# ENT-16 — Enterprise Foundation Closure GO/NO-GO

Durable lock: `docs/architecture/enterprise-foundation-closure-go-no-go.md`.

- ENT-16 is the **closure** of the ENT-1..ENT-16 enterprise foundation sequence.
  It adds a real, testable GO/NO-GO gate — not docs-only. Enforced by
  `foundation:enterprise-closure-check --strict`.
- Closure is **read-only**: it aggregates the sibling ENT-5..15 governance
  decisions and static config/file postures. It never runs a deploy, backup,
  restore, load test, or migration, and never weakens a sibling gate to reach GO.
- Decision is explicit **GO / WATCH / NO-GO**. GO only when every mandatory
  ENT-5..15 gate is GO, ENT-1..ENT-16 are completed with GO tags, all 13 closure
  criteria are met, evidence/safety/CI wiring + scripts + runbooks are present,
  the final `enterprise-foundation-go` tag is declared, and next sprint is not
  stale. NO-GO on any failing gate, unmet criterion, missing wiring, destructive
  drift, or secret/PII. WATCH only for a configured non-blocking condition;
  `--strict` blocks on WATCH.
- After ENT-16, `next_recommended_sprint` is **MON-1** (never a completed ENT-16).
  There is no ENT-17. On GO, the final `enterprise-foundation-go` tag ends the
  initial Enterprise Foundation Freeze.
- All later work inherits ENT-5..16: queue retry/idempotency, developer console
  read-only + audit, minimal health endpoints, PII/KTP/NIK masking, CI/CD +
  release-evidence + release-safety gates, backup-first deploy, rollback without
  auto data restore, restore rehearsal non-production only, load test
  non-production only, scale projection modeled/estimated, mandatory docs/runbooks;
  queue worker stays not-enabled unless a later approved sprint rolls it out.
- Destructive literals (`migrate:fresh`, `db:wipe`, `schema:drop`,
  `migrate:reset`) live in `config/enterprise_foundation_closure.php`, not scanner
  code. Docs never contain secrets, credentials, the environment file, or unmasked
  KTP/NIK; every closure doc passes the release-evidence forbidden scan.
- Evidence `enterprise-closure-check.json` is required in ci/vps profiles and as a
  release-safety pre-deploy gate; not committed to git.
